; Lazy emission and the class facts: the functions that only a vtable, a VTT
; or a construction vtable names (overriders, the destructor variants, the
; deleting destructors, thunk targets, the constructors of virtual bases) are
; reachable through the edges finish adds from the class facts, so none of
; them is dropped.  Three streams of the S2 and S3 tests: a diamond with a
; virtual base (VTT and construction vtables), covariant returns through
; virtual bases (thunks), and RTTI with a hierarchy (typeinfo, structors).
; The assembly is the same as with eager bodies.
; RUN: %ecil-asm %S/cxx-s2-diamond.test -o %t.diamond.ecil
; RUN: %edg-cir --stats --emit=asm -o %t.diamond.s %t.diamond.ecil 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DIAMOND
; RUN: %edg-cir --eager-bodies --emit=asm -o %t.diamond.e.s %t.diamond.ecil
; RUN: cmp %t.diamond.s %t.diamond.e.s
; RUN: %ecil-asm %S/cxx-s2-covariant-vbase.test -o %t.cov.ecil
; RUN: %edg-cir --stats --emit=asm -o %t.cov.s %t.cov.ecil 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=COV
; RUN: %edg-cir --eager-bodies --emit=asm -o %t.cov.e.s %t.cov.ecil
; RUN: cmp %t.cov.s %t.cov.e.s
; RUN: %ecil-asm %S/cxx-s3-rtti.test -o %t.rtti.ecil
; RUN: %edg-cir --stats --emit=asm -o %t.rtti.s %t.rtti.ecil 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RTTI
; RUN: %edg-cir --eager-bodies --emit=asm -o %t.rtti.e.s %t.rtti.ecil
; RUN: cmp %t.rtti.s %t.rtti.e.s

; DIAMOND: stats: lazy bodies: 15 deferred, 15 replayed, 0 dropped
; COV: stats: lazy bodies: 15 deferred, 15 replayed, 0 dropped
; RTTI: stats: lazy bodies: 16 deferred, 16 replayed, 0 dropped
